{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And with טחורים.</b> These are צריבים that emerge from the hidden place; therefore it says <b>בעפלים</b>, from the language of ״ויבא אל העופל״, and they are called piles (פי״ק) in Old French." "<b>Which you will not be able to heal.</b> Once the Holy One, blessed be He, strikes — who can heal?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "צריבים is retained untranslated as a technical term for inflamed swellings; פי״ק renders the Old French gloss for piles/haemorrhoids."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:32.966707421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}